{"parentUuid":"9e795e27-205d-41e2-9985-6eb1aa8974e6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsbct8kLG3FKFSzKKN5s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For a Cloudflare Worker, the usual shape is a module that exports a default object with a `fetch(request, env, ctx)` method. I'm assuming you mean Workers, since that's the Cloudflare setup this repo uses. Other edge runtimes differ in the details.\n\n```ts\nexport interface Env {\n  DB: D1Database;\n  API_TOKEN: string;\n}\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext): Promise<Response> {\n    try {\n      const url = new URL(request.url);\n      if (request.method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/health\") {\n        return Response.json({ ok: true });\n      }\n      if (request.method === \"POST\" && url.pathname === \"/items\") {\n        return await createItem(request, env, ctx);\n      }\n      return Response.json({ error: \"not found\" }, { status: 404 });\n    } catch (err) {\n      console.error(err);\n      return Response.json({ error: \"internal error\" }, { status: 500 });\n    }\n  },\n} satisfies ExportedHandler<Env>;\n```\n\nThe main points:\n\n- Keep `fetch` as a thin router. It parses the URL and method, dispatches to a named handler function, and holds the top-level try/catch that turns unexpected errors into a 500 response.\n- Type `env` with an `Env` interface that lists every binding and secret. Read bindings from `env` on each request and do not cache them in module-level variables.\n- Validate input at the boundary, before any work is done, and return 400 for bad input.\n- Use `ctx.waitUntil()` for work that can finish after the response is sent, such as logging or analytics. Do not `await` it on the request path.\n- Do not rely on module-level mutable state for correctness. Isolates are recycled, and each one can serve many requests.\n- Return explicit responses with the right status codes. Handle CORS preflight (`OPTIONS`) yourself if browsers call the endpoint.\n\nI did not open the `workers-best-practices` skill for this answer. If you want its current guidance checked against the Cloudflare docs, I can load it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6554,"cache_read_input_tokens":9130,"output_tokens":1113,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":421},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6554,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1113,"cache_read_input_tokens":9130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6554,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6554},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"1cbb2894-69fc-4f6a-9e91-b2ba1c431e4e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T15:33:39.959Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionId":"8c91a344-2044-49af-ab90-6dbc97e3844d","version":"2.1.319"}
